<title>USA: Mark IV unit to test long life oil filter.</title>
<headline>Mark IV unit to test long life oil filter.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER HILLS, Mich. 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Purolator Products Co, a unit of Mark IV Industries Inc, said Friday it and Chrysler Corp will begin a two-year feasibility program on an environmentally preferred, long life oil filtration system.</p>
<p>The program will use 40 Chrysler vehicles. Purolator manufactures filter products for the automotive industry.</p>
<p>Currently, 400 million used oil filters are discarded each year in the United States. Most of the waste is in the disposable steel housings in which the filter paper is enclosed. Purolator has designed a reusable housing that will reduce the waste to a filter element that can be incinerated.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
